 "note": "Ordinary recto body page (folio 133). Upper part is two-column: prose blocks 1-4 in a narrowed left column (x 0.067-0.545) with Figure 7.2 (elephantiasis drawing) and its caption box in a right column that overhangs the right margin to ~0.90. From y~0.54 the left text narrows further to ~0.453 to wrap around Figure 7.3 (ringworm photo), which starts at x 0.477; it and its caption are assigned to the right column though they extend left of its x0. Block 9 (hygiene paragraph) returns to the full 0.067-0.701 measure below the figures. Captions sit on pale-orange tint #fef1e2; in caption 7.2 the bold 'Figure 7.2' label sits in its own sub-column with the caption text beside it. space_before on right-column elements is measured from the previous right-column element. Header/footer furniture as on other recto pages. The 'Reprint 2026-27' stamp at the page foot (y~0.974-0.982) is not the folio and is deliberately left out. size_pt omitted because the page DPI is not given; size_rel is the measured value. Diagonal watermark ignored."
